add(f'Against fair prior Ink, {fresh_cells} fresh cells per CPU row are measured below. **Broad superiority over optimized handwritten JS, Rust or Wasm remains unproven.** All {v["regressions_retained"]} fresh adverse comparisons are retained; profitability is measured separately from correctness.\n')
add('## General equalities and proof sketches\n')
add('| Family | Equality | Conditions |\n|---|---|---|\n| Complementary cardinality | `count(filter(xs,p)) + count(filter(xs,not p)) = count(xs)` | U64 wrapping count; pure total predicate; U32/I32/F32/Bool elements; U64-element endpoint shared old consequence |\n| First accepted value | `filter(xs,p).at_or(0,z) = foldr(xs,z,x=>a=>choose(p(x),x,a))` | U32/I32/U64/F32; pure total predicate |\n| Mapped first accepted value | `filter(xs,p).map(f).at_or(0,z) = foldr(xs,z,x=>a=>choose(p(x),f(x),a))` | Same numeric types; pure total mapper; deployment composition |\n| Unused aligned prefix state | `scan(xs).zip(xs,(_,x)=>g(x)) = map(xs,g)` and symmetric zip | U32/I32/U64 scan; pure total mapper |\n| First prefix value | `scan(xs).at_or(0,z) = xs.at_or(0,z)` | Wrapping U32/I32/U64 scan |\n')
add('Complementary cardinality uses list induction and a case split on each predicate value. Exactly one partition gains a member; their U64 counts add to the original length modulo 2^64. The U64-element endpoint also has a checked old-only route through prior constant-sum, partition and mapped-sum laws; that route is offered symmetrically. Its old proof does not instantiate a U64 list variable with another list element type.\n')
add('First-match induction keeps the head when it satisfies the predicate, otherwise the tail answer. The mapped deployment composes the first-match equality with a checked map/fold transport. Frozen selected right-fold bodies visit every input word and evaluate the mapper on every accepted word, including values that are later replaced. Expert controls stop at the first accepted element and map only that element. These laws remove arrays; they do not prove early-exit performance. Pure total callbacks permit removal/interleaving of unobserved calls. Primitive grouping and the selected F32 value remain exact.\n')
add('Scan projection induction generalizes the scan accumulator to arbitrary initial state. A callback ignores that state and returns a function of the aligned original element, so one direct map replaces scan and zip. Six initial-state supports are counted separately. First-prefix lookup follows from the scan head at zero initial accumulator and preserves the empty default. The existing typed checker rejects F32.scan and Boolean numeric fold; these failed probes are preserved and no unsupported deployment is claimed.\n')
add('Sources: [skip proofs](../../knowledge/producers/web_skip23_laws.py), [pipeline proofs](../../knowledge/producers/web_pipeline23_laws.py), [source certificates](../../knowledge/producers/web_static23_laws.py). All objects are admitted using ordinary small-kernel proof rules, without trusted theorem flags, export-name whitelists or new optimization-specific kernel rules. Author evidence includes hash-valid false laws, actual interpreter values and typed source reification; complete target outputs are independently checked before timing.\n')
add(f'Historical snapshot `{m["prior_snapshot"]}` retains 1,648 entries. Fair prior `{m["effective_prior_snapshot"]}` has {c["effective_prior_entries"]} entries; current `{m["new_snapshot"]}` has {v["catalog_entries"]}. Both stores receive identical bounded old-only source-certificate opportunities, up to four source applications and 128 expanded bodies per task. Every type-indexed discovery root is checked in deterministic dependency-closed batches, and every proposed/final selection is replayed against its authenticated minimal closure. No root is silently omitted; the checker, planner search, costs and limits remain unchanged.\n')
