add('Literal JS/Rust controls retain eager source stages. Strong controls erase complementary predicate and unused prefix work, perform forward early-exit lookups, evaluate only the returned mapper, and may reuse vector destination scratch. Captured and borrowed JS, Wasm complete calls, native resident and input-snapshot calls have separate boundaries. Required input copies, output allocations, complete result consumption and cleanup are timed. GPU calls include upload, dispatch, readback and consumption. Fallback requests are not actual GPU samples. No handwritten WGSL expert is measured.\n')
